name valley_far
describe A 300 m view down a valley. The distance/LOD look shot: everything past the finest ring is a coarser node, so this is where the LOD ladder's seams, the moire Prompt 005 is about, and the fog Prompt 007 derives all become visible at once.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa

# Prompt 007 goal 344: --no-wind, and it is a CAPTURE-REPRODUCIBILITY requirement rather than a
# preference. Goals 333/335/338 put moving content in every frame -- a ground shimmer, swaying trees
# and grass -- driven by an animation clock that is the WALL CLOCK by default, so a golden of this
# pose stopped being reproducible. `--anim-step` makes the clock deterministic per FRAME and that is
# not enough on its own, because `capture end` lands on a different frame index between runs (goal
# 337 records that limit). Killing the wind for a golden-comparing capture is what the project
# already does for every wind A/B -- goal 332's own 0.0012% number was measured that way -- and it
# leaves the golden measuring everything else: terrain, tree shape, grass geometry, shading, LOD.
option --no-wind

pose_ground 48,0 -90 -8 12
wait 2

capture end valley_far

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6

# ------------------------------------------------- Prompt 005 goal 291: the ALIASING gate
# A DIFFERENT question from contrast_percent above, and the two move in opposite directions:
# contrast_percent asks "is there texture", moire_ratio asks "how much of that texture is
# energy piled against the pixel Nyquist limit rather than spread over resolvable
# frequencies". A deliberate stipple raises the first and leaves the second alone; aliasing
# raises both. Gate on both or a change that trades one for the other passes unnoticed.
#
# CALIBRATED, and this metric is far tighter than the GPU-time gate above because it is a
# DETERMINISTIC IMAGE MEASUREMENT rather than a clock reading -- no boost state, no
# contention. Three consecutive runs:
#   measured 1.771, spread under 0.05%
#   with --no-filter-albedo (goal 278 off): 4.333
# The gate is 2.1 -- about 1.2x the measured value, and it FAILS at 4.333, which is
# goal 291's own falsification and was verified by running it rather than assumed.
assert moire_ratio < 2.1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ goal 273: the regression gate
# A PERCENTILE of the GPU timestamp range across this fixed camera path, per research section 6.8 --
# never a mean (one hitch moves it) and above all never fps, which this machine's 165 Hz
# FIFO_RELAXED panel caps at 155-159 and which therefore cannot express a regression at all.
#
# PER BACKEND, because vk and d3d12 differ by 30-35% here and `ctest -L scenario` runs vk ONLY. A
# single threshold would have to be set by the slower backend, leaving the faster one 35% of slack
# -- a 30% vk regression would sail straight through the gate that CI actually runs.
#
# Each number is ~1.2x the worst of three runs on THAT backend: the smallest margin that survives
# run-to-run noise and still fails when the budget is tightened by 20%, which is goal 273's own
# Check and is demonstrated in the log.
#
# AND THE MEDIAN HERE, not the p95. This scenario runs ~320 frames, where the 95th percentile is the
# sixteenth-worst frame and therefore one hitch away from anything. Measured on BOTH backends:
#
#   vk    p95 4.76 3.68 3.53 (35% spread)  |  median 2.93 3.02 3.00 (3%)
#   d3d12 p95 4.45 4.93 5.92 6.46 (45%)    |  median 3.78 3.95 3.98 4.03 (7%)
#
# The long scenarios above gate on p95, where it holds to 2%. A p95 needs roughly 800 frames on this
# machine before it is a statistic rather than a coin flip -- the table lives in
# dev/scenario/include/dev/scenario/assertion.hpp.

# ------------------------------------------------ Prompt 007 goal 344: RECALIBRATED, not relaxed
# Same reason as stress_pose's: goal 329's 4 km region. Re-measured on the shipped default, three
# runs each:
#
#   vk      median 5.76 5.78 5.79    p95  9.19 10.74 12.09
#   d3d12   median 8.49 9.00 9.01    p95 11.49 16.92 17.85
#
# The MEDIANS are tight (vk within 0.5%) and the p95s are not, on either backend -- this pose's tail
# is the capture frame, which does a staging copy plus a WaitForIdle plus a libpng encode and is not
# a normal frame (CLAUDE.md records it at 200+ ms). So this scenario gets a median gate only, which
# is the metric goal 273 found carries the regression signal anyway.
#
# AND A SEPARATE NOTE ON THE MOIRE GATE BELOW, because it went the other way: it was failing at
# 2.304 before this prompt and now measures 1.872. Nothing about the aliasing changed -- goal 336
# found that the harness was resolving `pose_ground` against the pre-Prompt-006 noise world, so this
# scenario had been shooting from a pose 35 m from the one it names. The gate was right; the camera
# was wrong.
assert gpu_ms_median < 6.7 vk
assert gpu_ms_median < 10.4 d3d12
